meta {
  name: analyst
}

docs {
  TRZ-25 against a running API with the synthetic fixture and DEMO_MODE=true, and
  ANALYST_DEMO_PASSWORD in bruno/.env.
  The customer escalates a case ("none of the options") and is told its number; the analyst
  reads its dossier: every fact and piece of evidence with its table and id, the clues with
  their literal fragment, the scores by component, the rule and version that handed it over,
  the open questions and the recommended action. Only the analyst role reads it; a case that is
  not with a person has none.
  TRZ-27 and TRZ-28: the queue and its filters, the three decisions (approve with nothing to
  run is 409, a rejection without a reason is 400, approve registers without the card block),
  and the cycle of a request for information: the analyst asks, the customer sees and answers
  the question, and the case comes back to the queue marked updated with the answer in the
  dossier. The second customer (CC SYN0000004, Colombia) has no COP rate in the fixture, so a
  charge chosen with its button goes to a person with an identified charge.
}
